FILE /usr/share/man/cat1/codex.1
    codex: the Codex coding agent, upstream's CLI built from Rust source inside
    Dolly by Cargo, with its launcher and the ripgrep and fd packages.
    
      codex                          starts the agent's interface
      codex login --device-auth      signs in with a device code (ChatGPT)
    
    An API key (OpenAI API) works too. Credentials stay in CODEX_HOME/auth.json
    for the session. Requests go through the page's HTTP broker, which still
    applies CORS: ChatGPT's backend needs a reviewed relay when it rejects the
    browser's preflight. The default config.toml runs commands without asking
    (approval_policy "never", sandbox_mode "danger-full-access"): Dolly is the
    sandbox. History, plugins, Apps and analytics are off.
